":"Borrowing more","c":"Spending","d":"Taxing","correct":"A","exp":"Debt servicing"},{"q":"A developing country is characterised by","a":"High per capita income","b":"Low per capita income, high poverty","c":"High industrialisation","d":"Low population","correct":"B","exp":"Developing"},{"q":"Economic growth is increase in","a":"Real GDP over time","b":"Population","c":"Prices","d":"Money supply","correct":"A","exp":"Growth = real GDP rise"},{"q":"Economic development includes growth plus","a":"Improvement in welfare / living standards","b":"Growth only","c":"Population only","d":"Prices only","correct":"A","exp":"Development broader"},{"q":"HDI measures","a":"Income only","b":"Health, education, income","c":"GDP only","d":"Population only","correct":"B","exp":"Human Development Index"},{"q":"Poverty trap is","a":"Cycle where poverty causes poverty","b":"High income","c":"Wealth","d":"Growth","correct":"A","exp":"Poverty trap"},{"q":"Malthusian theory says population grows","a":"Arithmetically, food geometrically","b":"Geometrically, food arithmetically","c":"Both arithmetically","d":"Both geometrically","correct":"B","exp":"Malthus: pop geometric, food arithmetic"},{"q":"Optimum population is population that gives","a":"Maximum output per head","b":"Maximum population","c":"Minimum output","d":"Zero output","correct":"A","exp":"Optimum population"},{"q":"Overpopulation means population is","a":"Below optimum","b":"Above optimum","c":"Equal optimum","d":"Zero","correct":"B","exp":"Overpopulation > optimum"},{"q":"Underpopulation means population is","a":"Above optimum","b":"Below optimum","c":"Equal","d":"Zero","correct":"B","exp":"Underpopulation < optimum"},{"q":"Labour force is","a":"Working age population willing and able to work","b":"Total population","c":"Employed only","d":"Unemployed only","correct":"A","exp":"Labour force"},{"q":"Dependency ratio is","a":"Dependents / Working population","b":"Working / Dependents","c":"Population / GDP","d":"GDP / Populati