ey is a measure of value because it","a":"Is used to compare prices","b":"Is scarce","c":"Is paper","d":"Is gold","correct":"A","exp":"Unit of account"},{"q":"If money supply increases faster than output, result is","a":"Deflation","b":"Inflation","c":"Recession","d":"Growth","correct":"B","exp":"Too much money → inflation"},{"q":"Velocity of money is","a":"Speed money changes hands","b":"Amount of money","c":"Interest rate","d":"Exchange rate","correct":"A","exp":"Velocity"},{"q":"Quantity theory of money: MV =","a":"PT","b":"PQ","c":"MT","d":"VP","correct":"A","exp":"MV=PT"},{"q":"A bank's reserves are","a":"Money kept to meet withdrawals","b":"Loans","c":"Profits","d":"Deposits","correct":"A","exp":"Reserves"},{"q":"Liquidity preference is demand for money for","a":"Transactions, precautionary, speculative motives","b":"Only transactions","c":"Only speculative","d":"Only precautionary","correct":"A","exp":"Keynes motives"},{"q":"Speculative demand for money is inversely related to","a":"Income","b":"Interest rate","c":"Prices","d":"Output","correct":"B","exp":"Higher interest → lower speculative demand"},{"q":"A rise in interest rate will cause investment to","a":"Rise","b":"Fall","c":"Stay","d":"Double","correct":"B","exp":"Higher cost of borrowing"},{"q":"Multiplier =","a":"1 / (1-MPC)","b":"1 / MPC","c":"MPC / MPS","d":"1 - MPC","correct":"A","exp":"Multiplier = 1/(1-MPC) = 1/MPS"},{"q":"If MPC = 0.8, multiplier is","a":"4","b":"5","c":"2","d":"0.8","correct":"B","exp":"1/(1-0.8)=5"},{"q":"MPC + MPS =","a":"0","b":"1","c":"2","d":"Infinity","correct":"B","exp":"MPC+MPS=1"},{"q":"Consumption function: C = a + bY, b is","a":"Autonomous consumption","b":"MPC","c":"MPS","d":"Income","correct":"B","exp":"b = MPC"},{"q":"Saving function: S = -a + (1-b)Y, (1-b) is","a":"MPC","b":"MPS","c":"APC","d":"APS","correct":"B","exp":"MPS"},{"q":"If income is 1000 and consumption is 800, APC is","a":"0.8","b":"1.25","c":"200","d":"0.2","correct":"A","exp":"APC = C/Y = 0.8"},{"q":"If income rises by 100 and consumption rises by 80, MPC is","a":"0.8","b":"0.2","c":"1.25","d":"80","correct":"A","exp":"MPC = ΔC/ΔY"},{"q":"Investment is spending on","a":"Consumption","b":"Capital goods","c":"Imports","d":"Wages","correct":"B","exp":"Investment = capital"},{"q":"Gross investment - Depreciation =","a":"Net investment","b":"Gross investment","c":"Consumption","d":"Saving","correct":"A","exp":"Net investment"},{"q":"A major determinant of investment is","a":"Interest rate and expected profit","b":"Consumption only","c":"Population","d":"Tax only","correct":"A","exp":"Investment determinants"},{"q":"Aggregate demand =","a":"C + I + G + (X-M)","b":"C + I + G","c":"C + I","d":"C + G","correct":"A","exp":"AD = C+I+G+(X-M)"},{"q":"Aggregate supply is","a":"Total goods/services supplied","b":"Total demand","c":"Total consumption","d":"Total investment","correct":"A","exp":"AS"},{"q":"In Keynesian model, equilibrium income is where","a":"AD = AS","b":"AD > AS","c":"AD < AS","d":"Saving = 0","correct":"A","exp":"AD=AS"},{"q":"Inflationary gap is when equilibrium income is","a":"Below full employment","b":"Above full employment","c":"At full employment","d":"Zero","correct":"B","exp":"Inflationary gap"},{"q":"Deflationary gap is when equilibrium income is","a":"Above full employment","b":"Below full employment","c":"At full employment","d":"Zero","correct":"B","exp":"Deflationary gap"},{"q":"A major tool to close inflationary gap is","a":"Increase government spending","b":"Reduce government spending / increase tax","c":"Reduce tax","d":"Increase money supply","correct":"B","exp":"Contractionary fiscal"},{"q":"A major tool to close deflationary gap is","a":"Reduce spending","b":"Increase spending / reduce tax","c":"Increase tax","d":"Reduce money supply","correct":"B","exp":"Expansionary fiscal"}]
